                    ↓
          Is user authorized?
                    ↓
          Is order valid?
                    ↓
          Is operation allowed?
                    ↓
          Execute
      NOTE : LLM should request an action; application should authorize the action.
    Tool allowlisting:
    Tool argument validation:
    Output validation:
    Monitoring and audit logging:
  NOTE: Never trust the LLM as the security boundary; enforce security before retrieval, before tool execution, and after generation.”    

24. How would you determine whether Prompt A is actually better than Prompt B?
Ans:  I would not decide based on which prompt looks better. 
      I would run both prompts against the same representative evaluation dataset and compare measurable outcomes.
     what could I measure:
        Accuracy / correctness, Groundedness, Latency, Token usage / cost.

25. How would you create a representative golden/evaluation dataset for prompt testing?
Ans: I would create a golden dataset that represents the real production workload, including normal cases, edge cases, failures, and adversarial inputs. Each test case should have the input, expected behavior/output, and evaluation criteria.
      Collect real-world use cases
      Cover different scenarios
      Define expected results
      Include negative/abstention cases
      Maintain a balanced dataset
    A good golden dataset is not just a collection of sample questions; it is a representative benchmark of the production workload with expected behavior and measurable evaluation criteria. 
    I would continuously update it using real production failure cases to prevent regressions.

